{title: 325 - Jesus, I My Cross Have Taken}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: A}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Gospel}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[A/E]Jesus, I my cross have taken, all to leave [G#dim]and follow Thee.
[Bm]All things [A]else I [G#dim]have [A]forsaken, Thou from hence my all shall be.
[G#dim]Perish [A]every fond ambition, [E/B]all [A]I've sought [G#dim]or hoped or known.
[A]Yet how rich [Bm]is my [E/B]condition! [A]God and Heaven [Bm]are [A]still mine [G#dim]own.

Verse 2:
[A/E]Let the world despise and leave me, they have left [G#dim]my Savior, too.
[Bm]Human [A]hearts and [G#dim]looks [A]deceive me; Thou art faithful, Thou art true.
[G#dim]O, 'tis [A]not [Bm]in grief [A]to harm me, while thy love [G#dim]is left to me;
[A]O, 'twere not [Bm]in joy [E/B]to [A]charm me, If that love [Bm]be [A]hid from [G#dim]me.

Verse 3:
[A/E]Soul, then know thy full salvation; rise o'er sin, [G#dim]and fear, and care;
[Bm]Joy to [A]find in [G#dim]every [F#m]station [A/E]something still to do or bear:
[G#dim]Think what [A]Spirit [Bm]dwells [A]within thee; Think [E/B]what [A]Father's [G#dim]smiles are thine;
[A]Think that Jesus [Bm]died [E/B]to win [A]thee, child of heaven, [Bm]canst [A]thou repine?

Verse 4:
[A/E]Haste then on from grace to glory, armed by faith, [G#dim]and winged by prayer,
[Bm]Heaven's [A]eternal day's before thee, God's own hand shall guide thee there.
[G#dim]Soon shall [A]close [Bm]thy earthly [A]mission, soon [E/B]shall [A]pass [G#dim]thy pilgrim days;
[A]Hope soon change [Bm]to glad [E/B]fruition, [A]faith to sight, [Bm]and [A]prayer to [G#dim]praise.
